    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d245">

                <pb facs="0232" n="222" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg222"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/12–1649: Circular telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Certain Diplomatic and
                        Consular Officers </hi><anchor n="72" xml:id="d245-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-12-16T03:00:00-05:00">December 16,
                            1949—3 a. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Since survey of opinion re question recog Chi Commie regime initiated by Top
                    Secret Depcirtel Aug. 19 5 a. m., situation has developed to point where now
                    appears India may recog before end Dec. UK <pb facs="0233" n="223"
                        xml:id="pg223"/> and Burma may recog simultaneously or shortly thereafter to
                    be followed by majority other countries throughout world with interests in
                    China, excepting Philippines, Republic of Korea and possibly Italy.</p>
                <p>Under these circumstances Dept desires ur estimate of effect on opinion in
                    country and/or Govt to which you accredited if (1) US shld join in early recog,
                    (2) US shld delay recog until great majority other countries have recognized,
                    (3) US shld indefinitely withhold recog.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d245-f1" n="72" type="source" xml:id="d245-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to Batavia, Bangkok, Karachi, Manila, New Delhi, Rangoon, Saigon, and
                    Singapore.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
